WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:35.120
Episode 20 - The Switched Script

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.100
Kyouko, why would Uncle Yukihiro have anything to do...

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.640
with a traveling circus?!

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.140
She doesn't even know her lines, yet she still walked on!

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.210
Why would she do something so stupid?!

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.620
I wonder what's happening in this scene...

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:54.510
I don't know my lines or what's supposed to happen.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.720
All I can be sure of is that I'm Chie.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.910
I'll have to play off the others. That's what I'll do!

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:02.500
I'll have to follow their leads.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.170
Your father brought shame to the name of the House of Kaidoji!

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.720
Here goes nothing.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.510
Half of your flesh and blood came from a woman of ill-repute!

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:23.280
That's right! In normal circumstances, a girl like you wouldn't even be...

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:25.260
At this point in the script, Chie breaks into a soliloquy...

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.880
about her heartache and unbearable sadness!

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:30.580
Don't you have anything to say for yourself, Chie?!

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.820
Yes, say something!

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.220
Something.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.610
"Something?"

00:02:55.330 --> 00:03:00.650
Saying that not only show that she can't answer their insults, but...

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.710
it also expresses her sadness and pain by biting on the flower.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:08.300
What do we do? How can we follow the script when Chie isn't saying anything?

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:17.500
Idiots. You fell into your own trap.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:29.250
Mr. Utahiko! Miss Kyou! Mother is calling for you.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.810
You're not meant to be on stage yet, Ayumi, so why have you...

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.800
Thanks for your help though!

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:42.400
Please hurry. It sounded urgent.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:49.990
Maya Kitajima. I never imagined we'd share the stage in a situation like this...

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:52.430
that we'd be struggling to keep a play going like this!

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:57.140
Just watch. I'll make this play work.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.710
Follow their leads... which means I now have to follow Ayumi.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:07.690
In the script, Chie's cousins recount the entirety of her sordid family history.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:10.930
Then, Chie runs off stage yelling that she's leaving the household.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.330
The dukes return and start planning to marry Chie off,

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.550
before she can cause a scene.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:22.600
This becomes the first crack in the foundation of the House of Kaidoji that will eventually destroy it.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:29.130
If we don't keep to the script, the whole play will fall apart.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.250
But she doesn't know her lines or the scenario.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:39.230
So how can I coax her rage out of her? How can I make her storm off stage?

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:51.210
What exactly do you intend to do with that flower?

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:54.580
Do you want to become an artist like your father?

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.980
Miss Chie, there are a few things I need to tell you and I want you to listen carefully.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.290
But, if you feel you need to voice your own opinions at any point,

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:11.320
please don't hold back.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.550
In turn, I'll respond to whatever you have to say.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:17.390
So I have to listen carefully.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.240
And voice my opinions without restraining myself.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:24.160
Ayumi's trying to get us through this scene by ad-libbing.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:29.600
Uncle Yukihiro ran away from the household and only returned...

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.780
when you were five years old.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:33.770
Your mother was a geisha from Fukagawa...

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.950
My mother was a geisha...

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:38.740
and my grandfather kept her and my father apart?

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.850
My father loved me, but...

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:45.760
Ayumi is telling me Chie's background!

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.000
But why?

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.490
When my uncle left the house again,

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.820
you were put in the care of a servant household and since then,

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:57.620
you've frequently been mistaken for a servant!

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:03.140
Well, you <i>do</i> look like one!

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:06.400
Are you trying to make Chie sad, Ayumi?

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:07.940
Or...

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:12.010
Here's a flyer for the show your father's starring in.

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.930
Have you seen it yet?

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.460
I've got it!

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:24.680
Your father must be great! They've even put his face on here.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:28.290
Yes. He's a fantastic father!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.800
I'm impressed. She's stood up to the challenge.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:39.630
I'm surprised you can say that when he chose to toss you aside and abandon you!

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:42.510
But he still cares for me!

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:45.970
And what about the honor of his house?

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:51.300
If you have no answer, you're just admitting that...

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.550
the honor of this house means nothing to you! Ingrate!

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:56.550
She's trying to provoke me into a fight. But why?

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:00.740
It is solely the grace of this house that has allowed you to find happiness!

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:03.600
You had a miserable life before, wearing filthy rags, but we took you in...

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.710
so you could live a life of luxury!

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:10.770
I'll try to match my reactions with hers.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:13.020
But my father left this house,

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.860
which must mean he wasn't happy here!

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:20.060
Are you suggesting that this household tore them apart?!

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.020
That's exactly what I'm saying!

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:21.760
Silence!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:29.760
If those two lose pace even for a moment, it'll be fatal!

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.900
But she needs to say that she doesn't want to live here anymore...

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:35.140
and storm off stage!

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.670
Both you and your father are a stain on this household!

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.740
That's it. Get angry.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:46.970
Protect yourself, protect your father and let yourself explode with rage!

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.560
He's a clown!

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:56.300
Is there no way to erase this blemish on our household's reputation?

00:07:57.550 --> 00:08:01.820
If my father and I are indeed... a stain on this household,

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:04.480
then why can't you just leave us alone?

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:08.850
Why did you bring my father back here and take me in?

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:10.990
Nobody loves us here!

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:15.730
We had no choice. You are our blood, after all.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:20.220
How dare you say such a thing when you've lived in luxury in the House of Kaidoji?!

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:26.400
Kaidoji, Kaidoji, Kaidoji! That's all you people ever think about!

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:29.720
I understand exactly why my father chose to leave this house!

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:33.340
Then, why don't you follow his lead?

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:36.140
Maybe you can go off and become a traveling performer as well.

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:40.600
Fine! I'll...

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:45.270
Oh... I almost said "I'll leave this house then!" Maybe...

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:50.020
Maybe that doesn't fit in with the plot of the play, though?

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.320
I'm scared.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:16.280
I'll leave this house then!

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.460
She said it! She made her say it!

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:25.420
Do as you wish! Go!

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:29.420
I have to storm off stage? Ayumi?

00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:42.080
What? Chie is leaving the house?

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:46.130
Well, she's Yukihiro's child, after all. An ingrate like her father.

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:51.780
We must marry her off before she causes any trouble.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:55.450
I see... it linked to this scene.

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:55.930
But sir, she's only fourteen!

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:05.680
If Ayumi hadn't slapped me like that, I never would have thought to...

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.510
You were spectacular, Ayumi!

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:12.470
You managed to extract that line from Chie!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.680
It hurts getting slapped, doesn't it?

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.830
Ayumi...

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.090
Ayumi!

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.440
Thanks for saving our hides back there!

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:35.260
I hope you've learned a lesson from this. Don't ever do something...

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:36.940
as stupid as switching someone's script again.

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.200
Maya Kitajima...

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:47.260
Your courage on stage is fearsome.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:49.240
We were equally matched.

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:54.360
My only advantage was that I knew the play.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:57.920
It was only a slight advantage, though.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.540
Just what I'd expect from you, Ayumi!

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:06.800
You were wonderful!

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:12.890
I was ready to try my hardest to act through that scene.

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:21.730
But led by Ayumi, Chie's true feelings rose up inside me and my only option was to get angry.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.520
She really is a genius.

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:26.550
I can never hope to be as good as her...

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.480
I can't beat her!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:31.450
I want to congratulate you, Ayumi!

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.730
Mother! Father!

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:37.450
Her father is a movie director and her mother is a superstar.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:41.100
And Ayumi herself is stunningly beautiful and a genius on stage.

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:43.930
God, you're so unfair!

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.170
Stop right there!

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:47.190
It's late and it's raining.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:48.050
Let me drive you home.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:51.300
I'm fine! I'd rather get soaked through!

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:54.100
Hey, what gives you the right to be so rude?!

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:57.790
His generosity doesn't fool me!

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:02.090
He's done all sorts of underhanded things in an attempt to crush the Tsukikage Acting Troupe!

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.950
It's all gone just the way you wanted: the troupe has fallen apart...

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.680
and Ms. Tsukikage is in the hospital!

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:11.140
Now all you have left to do is steal the rights to <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>!

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.640
That's right. That's it exactly.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:20.340
If I want something, I won't let anyone get in my way.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:23.330
That's what you want to hear, isn't it?

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:33.920
What a horrible, horrible man!

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.890
I'll never forget this!

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:41.800
Your behavior seemed a little strange today.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:44.090
Losing your cool like that in front of everyone.

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:47.900
I see. So you were protecting that girl, Maya Kitajima.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:50.860
I didn't want the whole play to fall apart just because...

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:54.340
she didn't know her lines.

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:57.210
Got it. Let's leave it at that, shall we?

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.260
But I have to admire her courage.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:01.870
She's certainly very careless if she's willing to tangle...

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:03.070
with the Demon of the Daito Theater.

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:04.090
A reckless girl indeed.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:06.210
Reckless?

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:10.440
If she wasn't, she wouldn't have run on stage the way she did.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:14.090
I've never met a girl like her.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:27.090
"I enjoyed <i>Muen Sakura</i>!"

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:29.690
"I can't wait to see your next play!"

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.110
Isn't it wonderful, Maya?

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:34.180
I found it by the front door this morning.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:37.880
He came and watched the show!

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.820
I heard there'd be a lot of talented people here,

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:50.430
but seriously, everyone looks out of this world.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.100
They take first prize every year!

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.860
Apparently, everyone in the group...

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:56.360
is extraordinarily talented and they have famous directors and actors as tutors.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.220
It's Kanaya!

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:01.450
She looks a bit plain for the leading star of a Theater Club.

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:02.760
Just watch. You'll see.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:04.350
She's coming! She's coming!

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:06.270
The old witch!

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:10.810
Hide the babies! Don't let the children out!

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:16.050
The Demon Hag!

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:19.550
The Demon Hag is here!

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:23.260
She's grotesque. She looks like a real demon!

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:31.650
Where are the babies? Where are the children?

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:35.070
<i>You're</i> the ones who turned me into a hag!

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:37.660
Right before he died, my son told me to eat his flesh...

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:40.020
and take revenge on the village!

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:43.180
It's impossible for you to kill me!

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.890
Wow. I didn't realize anyone could be this convincing...

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.730
Wait a minute. I think I've seen that person before at the basement theater.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:59.600
I wish you luck in your new school.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:01.020
From Your Fan.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:04.050
PS: I hope the uniform suits you!

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.680
He's here! He's here in the school!

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:10.290
Please don't go anywhere!

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.430
I hope he's still around!

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.500
Then, he went to see the principal...

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:22.520
He was sitting in that car!

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:31.170
He's behind this door.

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:35.210
He's right behind this door.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:39.180
I'm finally going to meet him!

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:50.140
Masumi Hayami?

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.520
I wasn't expecting to see you here, little one.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:55.420
Is there something you need?

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:57.100
This man is rather an important guest.

00:15:57.590 --> 00:16:01.330
I'm a new student here! My name is Maya Kitajima.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:05.140
Has anyone come by here carrying a bouquet of purple roses?

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:07.100
Purple roses?

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:14.370
Well, he's the one who got me into this school...

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:16.770
and I really wanted to thank him personally.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:19.260
So, why did you come here?

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.260
I saw a rose in the car parked outside.

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:26.890
That's the Daito Corporation's car.

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:33.910
Well... Just before coming here, I gave a lift to an actress.

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:37.690
She was carrying a bouquet so I guess it must have fallen out then.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:39.160
Oh, I see.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:42.180
I just wanted to say thank you.

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:46.960
I'm sure that person knows how you feel.

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:50.720
By the way, your uniform suits you.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.900
Oh... thank you.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.690
I have to go. Excuse me!

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:59.100
Why won't you show yourself?

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:01.240
I really want to thank you.

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:06.600
<i>The Miracle Worker?</i>

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:10.600
It's the Daito's season opener.

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:15.160
We've actually done some secret pre-casting already and have narrowed the candidates...

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:19.010
for the lead role down to five people.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:24.040
Maya Kitajima, will you audition for the role of Helen Keller?

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:30.410
Helen Keller can't see, hear nor speak.

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:31.720
She was deafblind.

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.020
Deafblind?

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:37.380
It's the heartwarming story of how she discovered the happiness being alive can bring...

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:40.490
after meeting her tutor, Annie Sullivan.

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:45.040
Don't worry about us, Maya.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:48.430
It's not an easy role, but you should audition for it.

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:50.230
Thanks, guys!

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:54.500
Who are the other candidates?

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.290
Let's see...

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:58.610
One is a member of the One Star Academy's Acting Club:

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:00.260
Emi Kanaya.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:01.940
Kanaya?!

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:07.060
Then, there's the famous Ayumi Himekawa.

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:11.140
Actually, the role of Helen's tutor, Miss Sullivan, will be played...

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:13.010
by Utako Himekawa.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.190
Ayumi's mother is playing that role?

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:18.060
She'll be one of the judges for the auditions of Helen.

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:22.180
Then, there's the Ondine Troupe's director, Mr. Hajime Onodera.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.350
Onodera?

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:29.290
He's the man who assisted Masumi Hayami in ruining the Tsukikage Acting Troupe!

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:31.710
The judging will be objective.

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:35.010
Just because her mother is one of the judges, Ayumi won't...

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:37.740
I'm sorry, but I'm going to have to refuse.

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:39.660
You should give it some thought.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:43.680
No, I won't do it! I already know how it'll turn out.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:48.000
Ayumi will definitely get the role.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:49.750
There's no way I can beat her!

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:54.850
You appeared in <i>Muen Sakura</i>, didn't you?

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.630
Did you forget that you were on probation?!

00:18:58.550 --> 00:19:00.140
I'm very sorry!

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:03.470
I also heard that Ayumi had to baby you on stage...

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:09.970
You were the one who let the doll's mask slip and for that reason,

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:13.740
I put you on probation so you could think about your immaturity!

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:15.690
And yet, you went out on stage anyway?!

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:19.050
Maya, you are expelled from this troupe.

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:21.230
Expelled?

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:23.620
Ma'am!

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:26.660
I'll give you one more chance.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.230
You can return to the troupe if you get a role in <i>The Miracle Worker</i>.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.980
You have to go up against Ayumi and the other candidates...

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.710
and win the role of Helen Keller.

00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:37.720
If you can't do that, I want you to leave the troupe without further notice.

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:48.560
You say you're going to leave, no matter what?

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.770
That's right, Father.

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:51.710
I've already decided.

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:56.840
Mother, I don't want anyone to accuse me of riding on your coat-tails to get the role of Helen.

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:00.860
I don't want it to have anything to do with being your daughter.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:04.230
I'm going to win the role on my own merit.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:05.910
That's why I'm leaving.

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:07.840
I'm going to stay at Uncle Azabu's apartment.

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:09.290
Ayumi.

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:10.820
Okay.

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:11.900
Utako!

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:16.400
I won't interfere with your life.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.210
Do your best.

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:20.340
I'll send the housekeeper round every three days.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.180
Thank you.

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:26.310
I'm going now. The next time we meet, it will be at the audition.

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:29.900
Good luck, Ayumi.

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:37.460
As her mother, shouldn't you be stopping her?

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:40.370
How can I?

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.300
That girl has so much pride.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:47.310
Do your best, Ayumi.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:51.310
I'll be watching all the contenders as actresses and picking fairly.

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:56.000
I'm going to get the role of Helen Keller, Maya Kitajima!

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:59.330
No matter what, I won't lose to you!

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:04.150
If I get expelled, where will I go?

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:06.090
What will I do?

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:08.910
I have nowhere else to go.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:11.450
I don't know how to do anything else.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:19.510
Helen Keller was deafblind which means she couldn't see, hear nor speak.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.560
I'll do it!

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:26.390
I'll give it my best shot, if there's even the tiniest chance of success!

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:31.550
I'll find it and keep going!

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:35.940
That's right. Acting is all I have!

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:37.360
Acting...

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:43.480
Maya is pinning all her hopes and dreams on one role. A role she has to battle Ayumi for.

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:48.400
Will she be able to win the role of Helen Keller?

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:15.370
Asa kara yoru made yoru kara asa made

